feat(vox-gui/memory): Improve accessibility of MemoryView components
scale: ~54 lines across 2 files [M]

- `MemoryView.tsx`:
  - Added `type="button"` to all interactive buttons for explicit semantic meaning.
  - Added `aria-pressed` to `CorpusChip` and `Auto-recall` toggle buttons to indicate their state.
  - Added `aria-label` to `CorpusChip` buttons for better screen reader context.
  - Added `aria-hidden="true"` to decorative icons within buttons to prevent screen readers from announcing them.
  - Added `aria-label="Recall query"` to the recall search input.
  - Added `aria-live="polite"` and `aria-label="Recall citations"` to the citations region.
- `MemoryView.test.tsx`:
  - Added tests to verify `type="button"` is present on all buttons.
  - Added tests to verify the recall search input has an accessible label.
  - Added tests to verify the `Auto-recall` toggle uses `aria-pressed`.
  - Added tests to verify the citations region is marked as a polite live region.

